# The Docker build context is the repository root, because the service depends
# on the analyzer crate by path. Without this file the context would be several
# gigabytes of build directories and would take longer to upload than to
# compile.
#
# Only what the build needs stays: pace-analyzer/ (the crate it links) and
# service/ (the crate being built).

.git
.github

# Secrets never belong in a build context, even when nothing copies them.
.env
.env.*

# Build outputs of every kind.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.astro
pace-sdk/build*/
pace-analyzer/target

# Nothing else in the repository is part of the image: the site, the SDK, the
# ports and the documents all ship elsewhere.
pace-sdk/
websites/
ports/
scripts/
docs/
*.md
*.jsonl
